# Firebase rules: deploy DES and PROD together

Whenever Firestore or Storage security rules are changed or synced, **deploy them to both Firebase environments in the same session**. Never leave only one environment updated.

## Projects

| Alias | Project ID | Environment |
|-------|------------|-------------|
| `tourai-dev` | `tourai-1f3d9` | DES (development) |
| `tourai-pro` | `tourai-production-7dabf` | PROD (production) |

Working directory for deploys: `D:\Proyectos\TourAI\firebase`

## Source of truth

Canonical rules live in:

- `D:\Proyectos\Documents\docs-firabase\Rules\firestore.rules`
- `D:\Proyectos\Documents\docs-firabase\Rules\storage.rules`

Before deploy, sync into `TourAI\firebase\` (copy from that docs folder, or use `Sync-FirebaseRulesFromLocalDocs` from `firebase/scripts/_common.ps1`).

## Required deploy sequence

```powershell
cd D:\Proyectos\TourAI\firebase
# sync rules from docs-firabase first
firebase use tourai-dev
firebase deploy --only firestore:rules --non-interactive
firebase use tourai-pro
firebase deploy --only firestore:rules --non-interactive
```

If Storage rules also changed, include `storage` (or deploy `firestore:rules,storage` on both aliases).

## Do not

- Deploy rules only to DES or only to PROD
- Edit `TourAI\firebase\firestore.rules` without updating the canonical file in `docs-firabase\Rules`
- Assume a previous deploy covered both environments — verify both in the same turn

## After deploy

Tell the owner that rules were released on **DES** and **PROD** (include project ids).
